# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Orlando A. Mendible-Barreto et al. (2026). A Machine-Learned Interatomic Potential Free-Energy Surface for the First Step of MIL-101(Cr) Secondary Building Unit Formation.
#   arXiv (Cornell University). doi:10.48550/arxiv.2609.38518  arXiv:2609.38518v1
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2609.38518v1 (sha256 cc141f36122f46ee...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 631 (Application/model instance). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/mendiblebarreto2026.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the MACE-POLAR-M foundation model evaluated zero-shot and
# its naive, LoRA and multi-head (replay) fine-tunes on 70 wB97M-V
# configurations from exploratory metadynamics of [Cr(H2O)6]3+ + BDC
# ligand exchange, with energy and force MAEs on the training data and the
# 70-structure held-out test set (Sec. 3.2). Free-energy surfaces and
# binding energies are property results.

